 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Logic",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Each gate drives its Y output LOW only when both A and B are HIGH; with either input LOW the output is HIGH."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input levels",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The 74AHC2G00 switches at CMOS levels that scale with VCC (VIH 3.85 V, VIL 1.65 V at 5.5 V). The 74AHCT2G00 switches at TTL levels, VIH 2.0 V and VIL 0.8 V, over its 4.5 V to 5.5 V supply; an input held at 3.4 V on it adds up to 1.35 mA of supply current per input at 25 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input tolerance",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "An input may sit anywhere from 0 V to 5.5 V in operation regardless of VCC, and input leakage is specified with VCC anywhere from 0 V to 5.5 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input edges",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Input rise and fall must be no slower than 100 ns/V at VCC = 3.3 V ± 0.3 V (74AHC2G00) and 20 ns/V at VCC = 5.0 V ± 0.5 V (both types)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Marking",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The top carries A00 (74AHC2G00) or C00 (74AHCT2G00). Pin 1 is identified at the lower left corner, under the code."
